---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ComingSoon from '../../components/ComingSoon.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Robotics — Use Case"
  description="Scene state for manipulation and navigation — deterministic, low-latency perception that runs on edge compute. One API replaces YOLO, SAM, and custom glue."
  canonicalPath="/use-cases/robotics"
  mdTwin="/use-cases/robotics.md"
>
  <div class="page">
    <a class="back" href="/use-cases">← Use cases</a>
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Robotics</p>
      <h1>Robots that understand before they act</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Deterministic, low-latency perception that runs on edge compute.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content">
      <p>
        General-purpose robots need to understand object relationships and predict the
        consequences of actions — not just detect what's in view. The current state of the
        art is a fragmented stack: YOLO for detection, SAM for segmentation, custom post-processing
        for relationship inference, and handwritten glue that breaks every time the environment
        changes. Each component adds latency, adds a failure mode, and adds a training budget.
      </p>
      <p>
        Darwin replaces that stack with a single API call. It runs on Jetson-grade edge hardware
        with 45ms p50 per-frame inference, produces deterministic outputs with calibrated
        confidence scores, and works zero-shot across environments. The same model that understands
        a warehouse picking task understands a kitchen manipulation task — because it learned
        to understand video, not to detect a specific set of objects.
      </p>

      <ComingSoon note="Robotics integration guide and edge deployment examples — coming during our August launch." />
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 128px 24px 192px; }
  .back { font-size: var(--fs-body-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); display: block; margin-bottom: 64px; }
  .back:hover { color: var(--color-signal); }
  .hero { margin-bottom: 80px; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-footnote);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-signal);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h1); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .lede { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .content p { font-size: var(--fs-body-lg); line-height: 1.75; color: var(--color-text-primary); opacity: 0.85; margin: 0 0 32px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { h1 { font-size: var(--fs-h2); } .page { padding: 88px 20px 128px; } }
</style>
